{"t": 1795072481.2758908, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The upgrade to PHP 8.3 on the dev environment caused a fatal error specifically related to the **limit-login-attempts-reloaded** plugin, resulting in a 500 error on the homepage. This matches the vendor’s requirement that this plugin be deactivated before PHP 8.3 is used.\n\nBecause dev is still failing, I cannot yet propose production changes (Rule R2). The next step is to fix the dev issue:\n\n1. **Deactivate limit-login-attempts-reloaded on dev** (this should resolve the fatal error).\n2. Re-run `check_dev_pages` to confirm the site works.\n3. If successful, we can then propose the production plan that includes deactivating the plugin first, upgrading PHP, and verifying.\n\nWould you like me to deactivate the plugin on dev now?"}
{"t": 1795072481.276244, "kind": "stop", "reason": "end_turn"}
